 "currentFromYear": 2025,
 "yearRule": "The Data Security and Protection Toolkit (DSPT) year rolls in June, so in the autumn most organisations' most recent published submission is still the previous year's. A supplier is read as CURRENT here when its published submission is 2025-26 (version 8) or later, and BEHIND when it is 2024-25 (version 7) or older, which means a whole cycle has passed without a publication. A supplier reading \"Not Published\" has a DSPT record with no published submission against it.",
 "claimRule": "DSPT status is self-assessed and self-submitted by the organisation, and this page reports only what DSPT had published on the date it was read. Nothing here says a supplier is unsafe, non-compliant or barred, and nothing here is an endorsement of a supplier that is current. It is a published fact you can raise, not a claim you make.",
 "matchRule": "Matching is an exact match on the normalised company name, tried against the supplier's own name and the curated alternative names held for it. There is no fuzzy matching, because a wrong match would put another company's assurance status on a supplier. Where a supplier's names reach more than one DSPT organisation it claims no status and is listed as ambiguous; where no name matches it is listed as unmatched.",
 "unmatchedRule": "No exact DSPT name match was found for these suppliers. That is not a failing and not a status: a supplier can be assured under a parent company's registered name, under a name spelled differently from the one it trades as, or be outside the scope of the toolkit altogether. It is a reasonable thing to ask about, and an unreasonable thing to assert.",
 "dsptNote": "Status is as published by DSPT on the checked date, for the organisation whose DSPT name exactly matches the supplier's own name or one of the curated aliases held for it; matchedOn gives the name that matched. Identity beyond the name match is not verified, and this is not an endorsement.",
